      "type": "string",
      "extract_value": "This section outlines two main hypotheses. The first hypothesis proposes that individuals with higher body appreciation will show less interest in cosmetic enhancements. The second hypothesis suggests that individuals with higher body appreciation will have a greater need for uniqueness, both generally and specifically in appearance. Both hypotheses explore interactions between body appreciation and sex.",
      "evidence_source": "Drawing on research and theory on interest in cosmetic enhancements and need for uniqueness, we proposed two hypotheses. First, we hypothesized that individuals with higher body appreciation would be less interested in cosmetic enhancements as compared to individuals with lower body appreciation. We explored interactions between body appreciation and sex. Second, we hypothesized that individuals with higher body appreciation would have a higher need for uniqueness, both general uniqueness and uniqueness specific to the appearance domain as compared to individuals with lower body appreciation. We explored interactions between body appreciation and sex.",
